\ Module A's stored quotations call its private{ } helpers from interpreted
\ bodies inside the runtime image. `hidden` exists only as A's private helper,
\ so it must resolve at all; `tag` collides with module B's public export, so
\ A's own helper must win while the entry's own `tag` still resolves B's.

use { a-hidden-quot: a-tag-quot: } "fixtures/own_module_image_private_a.1z" ;
use { tag: } "fixtures/own_module_image_private_b.1z" ;

a-hidden-quot call print-line
a-tag-quot call print-line
tag print-line
